course: dictionary
lesson: 5365
title: One word, many meanings: kit
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. Kit is a good example. It can mean a set of things kept together for a job, a set of parts you build, the clothes and equipment for a sport, or a baby animal.
explain: «Pool test kits compare the colour of a water sample with drops added to a colour card.» The clues are compare, drops and colour card. So a kit here is a set of things kept together for a test. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "a set of things kept together for a test" still makes sense.
explain: «Don't forget your PE kit» is about school. PE is sport, so kit means the clothes and equipment you wear for sport. The same meaning appears in «the way a footballer has home kit and away kit and wears each at the right match», where wears and match are the clues.
explain: «A calm kit is a small set of things that help when feelings get big.» Here the words small set of things tell you that kit means a set of things kept together to help. When a word has more than one meaning, try each one in the sentence and keep the one that fits.
fact: «Kit» can be a noun (a kit, some kits) or a verb: «kit out» means to give someone the equipment they need (British English).
fact: A «first aid kit» is a set of things kept together for helping people who are hurt.
fact: A «model kit» is a set of parts you put together to make something.
fact: In British English, «PE kit» means the clothes and equipment you wear for sport.
fact: A kit is also a baby fox, rabbit or other small animal.
exercise: «Pool test kits compare the colour of a water sample with drops added to a colour card.» In this sentence, what is a test kit? | *A set of things kept together for a job | A small animal | A model aeroplane | A kind of swimsuit
exercise: «Don't forget your PE kit.» What does kit mean here? | *The clothes and equipment you wear for sport | A box of tools for a repair | A set of parts you put together | A baby rabbit
exercise: A kit is also a baby fox, rabbit or other small animal. Which meaning of kit is about an animal? | Clothes for a football match | *A baby fox, rabbit or other small animal | A first aid box | A set of parts you build
test: «A calm kit is a small set of things that help when feelings get big, such as a stress ball and a breathing card.» In this sentence, what does kit mean? | Sports clothes | A model you put together | *A set of things kept together to help | A baby animal
test: Which phrase means to give someone the equipment they need? | wear out | *kit out | pack in | give up
exam: Which best explains kit in «Don't forget your PE kit»? | A set of tools for a science test | *The clothes and equipment you wear for sport | A baby fox | A model you build at home
